        "subtitle": "Effective Date: 21 July 2025",
        "description": "<p><strong>Hamaragharr Vastu Corporation</strong> (\"we,\" \"us,\" or \"our\") respects your privacy and is committed to protecting it through this Privacy Policy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you visit our website <strong>www.hamaragharr.in</strong></p><p>Please read this Privacy Policy carefully. If you do not agree with the terms of this Privacy Policy, please do not access or use our Platform.</p><h3>1. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h3><p>We reserve the right to modify this Privacy Policy at any time. Any changes will be effective immediately upon posting the updated Privacy Policy on the Platform. Your continued use of the Platform after such changes constitutes your acceptance of the revised Privacy Policy. We encourage you to review this page periodically.</p><h3>2. Information We Collect</h3><p>We may collect information about you in the following ways:</p><h4>a) Personal Data</h4><p>Personal information you voluntarily provide, including but not limited to:</p><ul><li>Name</li><li>Email address</li><li>Phone number</li><li>Shipping and billing address</li></ul><p>This information is collected when you register, place an order, contact us, participate in surveys, contests, promotions, or interact with features of the Platform. Providing personal information is optional, but refusal may limit access to certain services.</p><h4>2.1) Derivative &amp; Log Data</h4><p>Information automatically collected when you access the Platform, such as:</p><ul><li>IP address</li><li>Browser type and version</li><li>Operating system</li><li>Access times</li><li>Pages viewed and referring URLs</li></ul><h4>2.2) Financial Data</h4><p>Payment-related information required to process transactions. We do not store complete payment card details. Payments are securely processed through third-party payment gateways:</p><ul><li>CC Avenue (Indian domestic payments)</li><li>CashFree (international payments)</li></ul><p>We encourage you to review the privacy policies of these payment processors.</p><h4>2.3) Social Media &amp; Third-Party Data</h4><p>If you connect your account through social media platforms (such as Facebook, Google, Instagram, etc.), we may collect basic public profile information as permitted by your privacy settings.</p><h4>2.4) Contests, Surveys &amp; Promotions</h4><p>Information provided when you participate in surveys, contests, or promotional activities.</p><h3>3. Principles for Protecting Your Data</h3><p>We adhere to the following data protection principles:</p><ul><li><strong>Lawfulness &amp; Fairness:</strong> Data is collected and processed lawfully and fairly.</li><li><strong>Purpose Limitation:</strong> Data is used only for specified, legitimate purposes.</li><li><strong>Transparency:</strong> You are informed about how your data is collected and used.</li><li><strong>Data Minimization:</strong> Only relevant data is collected.</li><li><strong>Security:</strong> Appropriate safeguards are applied to protect your data.</li></ul><h3>4. Use of Your Information</h3><p>We may use your information to:</p><ul><li>Create and manage your account</li><li>Process orders, payments, and refunds</li><li>Provide customer support</li><li>Improve our website</li><li>Send service-related communications</li><li>Share updates, offers, and promotional content</li><li>Conduct analytics and research</li><li>Prevent fraud and ensure platform security</li><li>Comply with legal obligations</li></ul><h3>5. Disclosure of Your Information</h3><p>We may share your information in the following circumstances:</p><h4>5.1) Legal Requirements</h4><p>When required to comply with applicable laws, court orders, or legal processes.</p><h4>5.2) Service Providers</h4><p>With trusted third parties who assist us in operating our business (payment processing, hosting, analytics, email services, marketing, and customer support).</p><h4>5.3) Business Transfers</h4><p>In the event of a merger, acquisition, restructuring, or sale of assets, your data may be transferred to the successor entity.</p><h4>5.4) With Your Consent</h4><p>For marketing or promotional purposes where permitted by law.</p><p><strong>We do not sell your personal data to third parties</strong></p><h3>6. Cookies &amp; Tracking Technologies</h3><p>We use cookies, web beacons, and similar technologies to:</p><ul><li>Enhance user experience</li><li>Analyze usage trends</li><li>Improve functionality</li></ul><p>You may manage cookie preferences through your browser settings. Disabling cookies may affect certain features of the Platform.</p><h3>7. Third-Party Websites</h3><p>Our Platform may contain links to third-party websites or services. We are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of such third parties. Please review their privacy policies before providing any information.</p><h3>8. Security of Your Information</h3><p>We implement reasonable administrative, technical, and physical security measures to protect your personal data. However, no method of transmission over the internet is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p><h3>9. Do-Not-Track Signals</h3><p>Currently, there is no universally accepted standard for Do-Not-Track (DNT) signals in India. Therefore, we do not respond to DNT browser signals at this time.</p><h3>10. Data Protection Rights (EEA Users)</h3><p>If you are a resident of the European Economic Area (EEA), you have the right to:</p><ul><li>Access your personal data</li><li>Correct inaccurate data</li><li>Request deletion of data</li><li>Restrict or object to processing</li><li>Request data portability</li><li>Withdraw consent at any time</li></ul><p>To exercise these rights, please contact us using the details below.</p><h3>11. Managing Your Information</h3><h4>Account Management</h4><p>You may update or delete your account information by:</p><ul><li>Logging into your account settings</li><li>Contacting us directly</li></ul><p>We may retain certain data as required for legal, regulatory, or fraud-prevention purposes.</p><h4>Email &amp; Communication Preferences</h4><p>You may opt out of promotional emails by:</p><ul><li>Updating your account preferences</li><li>Using the unsubscribe link in our emails</li><li>Contacting us directly</li></ul><h3>12. Contact Us</h3><p>If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, please contact us:</p><p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href=\"mailto:support@hamaragharr.in\">support@hamaragharr.in</a><br><strong>Phone:</strong> +91 8130340819<br><strong>Support Hours:</strong> Monday to Saturday, 10:00 AM to 6:00 PM</p><p><strong>Hamaragharr Vastu Corporation</strong><br>Faridabad Sector 21c Haryana<br>Haryana, India</p>",
